-- models/engine/delta-model.rofl — HYPOTHESES ABOUT A DELTA, AS RULES THE DELTA'S OWN FACTS JUDGE. Loaded beside the
-- rules of a world (no corpus: the reflection of the rules is what it reads) and the facts a delta of that world
-- wrote under ROFL_DELTA_FACTS (rust/rofl/src/engine/meter.rs): out, kept, back, tries per relation; whole, keyed per
-- rule; step, moved per step of a volume. Everything here is in the book `delta`.
--
-- A FORECAST says from the shape of the rules what a delta must do; a VERDICT sets it beside what the delta did:
--   whole_by_shape(R, Rel)   an aggregate whose key a change of Rel does not name: the rule is withdrawn and fired
--                            over the whole store (Eval::agg_keys gives the key up)
--   returns_by_shape(Rel)    a relation recursive with itself: a fact of it that loses a firing is never kept in
--                            place (Eval::overdelete), it goes and is derived again where it still holds
--   every copy returns        a copy taken out of a volume is laid there again where a volume still makes what it
--                            copies (Volumes::pass_on): none is owed when the rounds end, and none stands
--                            that no volume makes (an orphan)
-- and the verdicts: `held` the forecast and the delta agree, `off` the forecast said it and the delta did not,
-- `unforeseen` the delta did it and no forecast said it. What is unforeseen is what the model has no word for yet.

edb(out). edb(kept). edb(back). edb(tries). edb(whole). edb(keyed). edb(step). edb(moved). edb(taken). edb(owed). edb(orphan). edb(seed). edb(read). edb(once). edb(walked). edb(spent). edb(counted).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the reflection, by slot
dm_lit[delta](R, K, Rel, As) :- premise_lit(R, K, L), L = $lit(Rel, _, As, _).
dm_agg[delta](R, K, Body)    :- premise_lit(R, K, L), L = $agg(_, _, _, _, Body).
dm_head[delta](R, Rel, As)   :- conclusion_lit(R, 1, L), L = $lit(Rel, _, As, _).
-- a literal inside an aggregate, by its place in the body
dm_in[delta](R, K, 1, B)     :- dm_agg[delta](R, K, B).
dm_in[delta](R, K, J, T)     :- dm_in[delta](R, K, I, $cons(_, T)), J is I + 1.
dm_inlit[delta](R, K, J, Rel, As) :- dm_in[delta](R, K, J, $cons(L, _)), L = $lit(Rel, _, As, _).
-- the variables of an argument list
dm_args[delta](As)           :- dm_lit[delta](_, _, _, As).
dm_args[delta](As)           :- dm_inlit[delta](_, _, _, _, As).
dm_args[delta](As)           :- dm_head[delta](_, _, As).
dm_tail[delta](As, As)       :- dm_args[delta](As).
dm_tail[delta](As, T)        :- dm_tail[delta](As, $cons(_, T)).
dm_has[delta](As, V)         :- dm_tail[delta](As, $cons($var(V), _)).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------- an aggregate fired whole, by shape
-- the key: a variable of the head that the aggregate's body names
dm_key[delta](R, K, V)       :- dm_head[delta](R, _, H), dm_has[delta](H, V), dm_inlit[delta](R, K, _, _, As), dm_has[delta](As, V).
-- a literal the rule reads, outside the aggregate or in it, that leaves a variable of the key free
dm_free[delta](R, Rel, V)    :- dm_key[delta](R, K, V), dm_inlit[delta](R, K, _, Rel, As), not dm_has[delta](As, V).
dm_free[delta](R, Rel, V)    :- dm_key[delta](R, _, V), dm_lit[delta](R, _, Rel, As), not dm_has[delta](As, V).
whole_by_shape[delta](R, Rel) :- dm_free[delta](R, Rel, _).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------ a relation that returns, by shape
dm_dep[delta](Rel, P)        :- dm_head[delta](R, Rel, _), dm_lit[delta](R, _, P, _).
dm_dep[delta](Rel, P)        :- dm_head[delta](R, Rel, _), dm_inlit[delta](R, _, _, P, _).
dm_reach[delta](Rel, P)      :- dm_dep[delta](Rel, P).
dm_reach[delta](Rel, P)      :- dm_reach[delta](Rel, Q), dm_dep[delta](Q, P).
returns_by_shape[delta](Rel) :- dm_reach[delta](Rel, Rel).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ verdicts
dm_moved[delta](Rel)         :- out[delta](Rel, _).
dm_moved[delta](Rel)         :- back[delta](Rel, _).
dm_moved[delta](Rel)         :- kept[delta](Rel, _).
dm_fired[delta](R, Head, N)  :- whole[delta](R, Head, N).
-- an aggregate the forecast names, over a relation the delta moved: it was fired whole
whole_held[delta](Head, R, Rel, N)   :- whole_by_shape[delta](R, Rel), dm_moved[delta](Rel), whole[delta](R, Head, N).
whole_off[delta](Head, R, Rel)       :- whole_by_shape[delta](R, Rel), dm_moved[delta](Rel), dm_head[delta](R, Head, _), not dm_fired[delta](R, Head, _).
whole_unforeseen[delta](Head, R, N)  :- whole[delta](R, Head, N), not whole_by_shape[delta](R, _).
-- a relation recursive with itself: nothing of it kept in place, and what went of it and came back
returns_held[delta](Rel, Out, Back)  :- returns_by_shape[delta](Rel), out[delta](Rel, Out), back[delta](Rel, Back), not kept[delta](Rel, _).
returns_off[delta](Rel, Kept)        :- returns_by_shape[delta](Rel), kept[delta](Rel, Kept).
-- taken out and derived again with no recursion to say why, and never once kept in place
returns_unforeseen[delta](Rel, Out, Back) :- out[delta](Rel, Out), back[delta](Rel, Back), not returns_by_shape[delta](Rel), not kept[delta](Rel, _).
-- the sum of it: of what the delta took out, how much it derived again, and how much of that a forecast names
back_total[delta](T)         :- T is sum(N ; Rel : back[delta](Rel, N)).
back_foreseen[delta](T)      :- T is sum(B ; Rel : returns_held[delta](Rel, _, B)).
back_unforeseen[delta](T)    :- T is sum(B ; Rel : returns_unforeseen[delta](Rel, _, B)).
-- a copy owed: the volume that read it counts and joins without it, and answers short
copy_owed[delta](Rel, N)     :- owed[delta](Rel, N).
-- a copy with no original: a volume reads a fact no volume makes
copy_orphan[delta](Rel, N)   :- orphan[delta](Rel, N).
copies_taken[delta](T)       :- T is sum(N ; Rel : taken[delta](Rel, N)).
-- what a volume loses as copies are laid into it: an addition takes out only what a new fact blocks or moves
lay_takes[delta](Cause, Rel, N) :- seed[delta](lays, Cause, Rel, N).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the weight
-- rows read are the weight of a delta: by step, by the relation a rule concludes, and the share of each in the whole
read_step[delta](Step, T)        :- read[delta](Step, _, _, _), T is sum(N ; R : read[delta](Step, R, _, N)).
read_total[delta](T)             :- T is sum(N ; Step : read_step[delta](Step, N)).
read_head[delta](Step, Head, T)  :- read[delta](Step, _, Head, _), T is sum(N ; R : read[delta](Step, R, Head, N)).
heavy[delta](Step, Head, T, Pct) :- read_head[delta](Step, Head, T), read_total[delta](All), All > 0, Pct is T * 100 / All, Pct >= 5.
-- what a rule fired whole weighs, beside the forecast that it would be
whole_weight[delta](Head, T)     :- whole[delta](R, Head, _), T is sum(N ; Step : read[delta](Step, R, Head, N)).
-- the forecast of the weight: what is heavy is what returns (a relation recursive with itself is taken out and derived
-- again); a heavy head that does not return is weight the model has no word for
heavy_held[delta](Step, Head, Pct)       :- heavy[delta](Step, Head, _, Pct), returns_by_shape[delta](Head).
heavy_unforeseen[delta](Step, Head, Pct) :- heavy[delta](Step, Head, _, Pct), not returns_by_shape[delta](Head).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the boundary of a volume
-- THE SAME EDIT TAKEN BY ONE WORLD, its facts loaded beside these in the book `alone` (the delta's facts with [delta]
-- written [alone]), is the delta with no boundary: no copy, no laying, no round. The forecast: a copy that is the
-- original (a volume reads the fact where it stands) leaves a delta of volumes only what the world alone does.
--   a fact goes once          what goes more than once goes so by the boundary: in several volumes, or round after round
--   no more goes              what volumes take out and the world alone does not is doomed by reach across the boundary
--   laying is the boundary    the world alone reads no more rows than the volumes read taking out and in
alone_out[delta](Rel, N)     :- out[alone](Rel, N).
alone_read[delta](T)         :- T is sum(N ; Step : alone_step[delta](Step, N)).
alone_step[delta](Step, T)   :- read[alone](Step, _, _, _), T is sum(N ; R : read[alone](Step, R, _, N)).
repeated[delta](Rel, N)      :- out[delta](Rel, O), once[delta](Rel, U), N is O - U, N > 0.
reach_more[delta](Rel, N)    :- once[delta](Rel, U), out[alone](Rel, A), N is U - A, N > 0.
reach_more[delta](Rel, U)    :- once[delta](Rel, U), not alone_went[delta](Rel).
alone_went[delta](Rel)       :- out[alone](Rel, _).
repeated_total[delta](T)     :- T is sum(N ; Rel : repeated[delta](Rel, N)).
reach_more_total[delta](T)   :- T is sum(N ; Rel : reach_more[delta](Rel, N)).
out_total[delta](T)          :- T is sum(N ; Rel : out[delta](Rel, N)).
alone_out_total[delta](T)    :- T is sum(N ; Rel : out[alone](Rel, N)).
-- the verdict of the third: the rows the volumes read outside the laying, beside the rows of the world alone
within[delta](T)             :- read_step[delta](takes_out, A), read_step[delta](takes_in, B), T is A + B.
laying_held[delta](Alone, Within)  :- alone_read[delta](Alone), within[delta](Within), Within >= Alone.
laying_off[delta](Alone, Within)   :- alone_read[delta](Alone), within[delta](Within), Alone > Within.
-- a fact that stands after the edit and went all the same: it went once or more and is back
once_total[delta](T)         :- T is sum(N ; Rel : once[delta](Rel, N)).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the world's part
-- AN EDIT COSTS BY THE EDIT: the forecast is that a delta walks no volume whole. A pass that does is off by the
-- records it walked, and beside them stand the facts the delta was given, to say how many times over.
walks_whole[delta](What, N)  :- walked[delta](What, N).
walked_total[delta](T)       :- T is sum(N ; What : walked[delta](What, N)).
given_total[delta](T)        :- moved[delta](takes_out, A), moved[delta](takes_in, B), T is A + B.

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- where the time is
-- THE TIME OF A DELTA IS WHERE ITS ROWS ARE READ: the forecast is that the parts whose rules read rows (a volume
-- takes out and in, a volume is laid copies) carry the time. A part of a twentieth of the time or more that reads
-- no row is time the model has no word for.
reads_rows[delta](out_and_in). reads_rows[delta](lays).
spent_total[delta](T)        :- T is sum(Ms ; What : spent[delta](What, Ms)).
long[delta](What, Ms, Pct)   :- spent[delta](What, Ms), spent_total[delta](T), T > 0, Pct is Ms * 100 / T, Pct >= 5.
time_held[delta](What, Ms, Pct)       :- long[delta](What, Ms, Pct), reads_rows[delta](What).
time_unforeseen[delta](What, Ms, Pct) :- long[delta](What, Ms, Pct), not reads_rows[delta](What).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ one dictionary of names
-- THE FORECAST OF ONE DICTIONARY (w_scroll_names), from what the volumes hold: a volume makes about 720 000 names above
-- the core and a thousand of them are in a fact, 25 000 compound terms and 20 000 of them in a fact; the names the
-- files spell are the core's already. So few of the terms a volume asks a neighbour for are numbered otherwise there,
-- and one dictionary takes little time off the plan of what to lay: it is the ground a premise read where it lies
-- stands on, not a gain of its own. `renamed_pct` is the share; the forecast holds under a tenth. (#225 before the
-- dictionary: 12 of a hundred, 1.5M of 11.9M terms asked, so the forecast was short by a little; with the dictionary
-- the share is nothing, and the plan's time says what it was worth.)
renamed_pct[delta](P)        :- counted[delta](term_asked, A), counted[delta](term_named_again, N), A > 0, P is N * 100 / A.
one_dictionary_gains_little[delta](P) :- renamed_pct[delta](P), P < 10.
one_dictionary_gains_much[delta](P)   :- renamed_pct[delta](P), P >= 10.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ a premise read in place
-- THE FORECAST OF READING A PREMISE WHERE IT LIES (w_scroll_foreign_premise), from the shape of the crossing: a copy
-- laid is found twice, once by the plan asking the neighbours' indexes on one thread and once by the rule that joins
-- it; what the rule then concludes is derived whichever way the premise is seen. So reading in place takes off the
-- plan and leaves the laying's firings: `in_place_gains[delta](Pct)` is the plan's share of the delta's wall parts,
-- the most it can give in time; what it gives in memory is the copies (`taken`, and the half of a volume that is
-- laid).
wall_part[delta](opens). wall_part[delta](gives). wall_part[delta](finds). wall_part[delta](dooms).
wall_part[delta](out_and_in). wall_part[delta](plans). wall_part[delta](lays). wall_part[delta](notes).
wall_part[delta](answers). wall_part[delta](keeps).
wall_total[delta](T)         :- T is sum(Ms ; What : spent[delta](What, Ms), wall_part[delta](What)).
in_place_gains[delta](Pct)   :- spent[delta](plans, P), wall_total[delta](T), T > 0, Pct is P * 100 / T.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- a premise looked up next door
-- THE FORECAST OF LOOKING A PREMISE UP IN THE NEIGHBOURS' FOLDS IN PLACE OF LAYING COPIES (w_scroll_foreign_premise),
-- from what a lookup's key names. A key that names a node of the volume's own files is answered at home, as now. One
-- that names a node of another file goes to that file's fold, one lookup more. One that names no node may be answered
-- in any fold: a lookup more in each of the others. The copies laid are what keeps every lookup at home, so the price
-- of having none is the lookups added, as a share of those made; the laying it would save is `laying_pct`. The counts
-- are of the first evaluation of the engine's own model, 123 files in 4 volumes (the ledger says how they were taken).
looked_up[volumes](no_node, 6126177). looked_up[volumes](node_at_home, 58612205). looked_up[volumes](node_away, 1385522).
laying_pct[volumes](14).
workers[volumes](4). workers[volumes](8). workers[volumes](12).
looked_up_total[volumes](T)      :- T is sum(N ; What : looked_up[volumes](What, N)).
lookups_added[volumes](K, Pct)   :- workers[volumes](K), looked_up[volumes](no_node, A), looked_up[volumes](node_away, B),
                                    looked_up_total[volumes](T), Pct is (A * (K - 1) + B) * 100 / T.
-- With an [index] that says in one look which folds hold a key that names no node, each such lookup is one look more
-- whatever the number of folds.
lookups_added_indexed[volumes](Pct) :- looked_up[volumes](no_node, A), looked_up[volumes](node_away, B),
                                    looked_up_total[volumes](T), Pct is (A + B) * 100 / T.
next_door_pays[volumes](K, Pct)  :- lookups_added[volumes](K, Pct), laying_pct[volumes](L), Pct < L.
next_door_costs[volumes](K, Pct) :- lookups_added[volumes](K, Pct), laying_pct[volumes](L), Pct >= L.

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------- a fact lies where its premises' files say
-- THE FORECAST OF AN ADDRESS THAT IS THE SET OF FILES A FACT WAS DERIVED FROM (the owner, 2026-11-12): a fold is a set
-- of files, a fact derived from premises in folds A and B lies in the fold of their files together, and an edit of a
-- file drops the folds whose set holds it and derives them again; the rest is not opened. Counted on the first
-- evaluation of the engine's own model, 123 files in one volume, by each fact's first firing (the ledger says how).
derived[folds](6352254). sets[folds](3493). largest_set[folds](16). in_one_file[folds](5177930).
in_two_folds[folds](35152).
-- an edit of the 7 files of #225: the folds whose set holds one, and the derived facts in them
edit_folds[folds](1657). edit_facts[folds](784748).
-- what the delta of today takes out for the same edit, and the time of the whole evaluation and of that delta, ms
taken_out_today[folds](59000). anew_ms[folds](45000). delta_ms[folds](15000).
-- the share of the world an edit derives again, and the time that is of the whole evaluation
edit_share[folds](Pct)   :- edit_facts[folds](E), derived[folds](D), Pct is E * 100 / D.
edit_ms[folds](Ms)       :- edit_share[folds](P), anew_ms[folds](A), Ms is A * P / 100.
-- the forecast holds while the folds are few beside the facts and the edit by folds is forecast under the delta of today
folds_are_few[folds](N)  :- sets[folds](N), derived[folds](D), N * 1000 < D.
folds_pay[folds](Ms)     :- edit_ms[folds](Ms), delta_ms[folds](T), Ms < T.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------- what goes is judged by the firings kept
-- THE FORECAST OF JUDGING AN OVERDELETION BY THE FIRINGS THE STORE KEEPS, from the shape of the overdeletion: it took
-- out whatever cited a fact gone unless a firing stood on premises outside the fact's own recursion, so in a recursive
-- relation one fact gone took the relation's reach with it, and each was derived again by solving its rules with the
-- head bound (`tries`), again and again while one before it on the chain was still out. A world keeps every firing,
-- so what stands can be read off them: of what the seeds reach, a fact with a firing over premises not reached, or
-- proved so before it, stands, and no rule is solved for it. What is left to try is what went and did not come back
-- by a firing it had. Counted on #225 in one store on one core, the delta of today (the ledger says how).
out_today[judged](704805). back_today[judged](679934). tries_today[judged](743431). in_ms_today[judged](91541).
-- at most what came back came by a firing it had: the tries left are at least what stayed out
tries_left[judged](N)   :- out_today[judged](O), back_today[judged](B), N is O - B.
in_ms[judged](Ms)       :- tries_left[judged](N), tries_today[judged](T), in_ms_today[judged](A), Ms is A * N / T.
judging_pays[judged](Ms) :- in_ms[judged](Ms), in_ms_today[judged](A), Ms * 4 < A.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------- a closure premise is led by its news
-- THE FORECAST OF READING A CLOSURE BY ITS NEWS, from the shape of two premises. A premise over a `nearest` whose rows
-- are stored facts was matched as a closure and so read every row, whatever the news were: its reads should be the
-- rows of the news. A new edge of a walked graph gives ancestors x descendants row seeds, and a rule that joins the
-- ancestor to the rest of its body solved the rest once a seed: solved once an ancestor, the seeds left are the rows
-- of the ancestors the rest of the body holds. Counted on #225 in one store on one core after [judged].
read_today[led](parent, 2200000). news[led](parent, 610).
read_today[led](at_step, 2070000). news[led](at_step, 7).
read_today[led](does_fn, 3250000). delta_ms_today[led](24000).
-- a news fact is read with the rows it joins: a hundred a fact is the bound on a tree of this size
read[led](R, N)     :- news[led](R, K), N is K * 100.
read_pays[led](R)   :- read[led](R, N), read_today[led](R, T), N * 10 < T.
-- gdb gave these three a third of the delta; led by the news they should leave at most a tenth of that
delta_ms[led](Ms)   :- delta_ms_today[led](T), Ms is T - T / 3 + T / 30.
-- measured after: the delta, and what the three still read
delta_ms_after[led](18464). read_after[led](parent, 0). read_after[led](at_step, 37752). read_after[led](does_fn, 1963514).
forecast_held[led](R)  :- read[led](R, N), read_after[led](R, A), A * 10 < N * 1000.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------- threads that write one scroll
-- THE FORECAST OF THREADS WRITING ONE SCROLL, from where a whole evaluation in one store spends its time on four cores
-- (60 samples of the thread that evaluates, #225's tree anew; the ledger says how): concluding is written by one
-- thread, and the threads that match stand parked nine samples of ten. A thread that owns a region of the scroll
-- concludes into it while the others conclude into theirs, and all read every region as the round began: what is
-- split is the matching and the concluding, what stays on one thread is the reading of the files and the rest.
sample[shared](concludes, 22). sample[shared](matches, 16). sample[shared](reads_files, 7). sample[shared](rest, 15).
anew_ms_one_store[shared](80000). anew_ms_volumes[shared](50000). threads[shared](4).
split[shared](concludes). split[shared](matches).
all[shared](N)        :- N is sum(K ; P : sample[shared](P, K)).
split_part[shared](N) :- N is sum(K ; P : sample[shared](P, K), split[shared](P)).
anew_ms[shared](Ms)   :- all[shared](A), split_part[shared](S), anew_ms_one_store[shared](T), threads[shared](C), Ms is T * (A - S) / A + T * S / A / C.
shared_pays[shared](Ms) :- anew_ms[shared](Ms), anew_ms_volumes[shared](V), Ms < V.
-- the first step: one worker, and the files' lower stage on the cores it leaves (one core: 13 samples of 60 in the
-- lower stage, 8 reading the files, 85 s)
lower_sample[shared](21, 60). anew_ms_one_worker[shared](85000).
anew_ms_lower_on_threads[shared](Ms) :- lower_sample[shared](L, A), anew_ms_one_worker[shared](T), threads[shared](C), Ms is T * (A - L) / A + T * L / A / C.
-- measured: one worker on four cores, anew and by delta, answers equal
anew_ms_lower_measured[shared](65250). delta_ms_one_worker[shared](18978).
-- a key a proof quotes (of an absence, of a closure's row) spelled once: 11 samples of 60 were in spelling them
-- (one worker, four cores, 65 s); at most those go
keys_sample[shared](11, 60).
anew_ms_keys_once[shared](Ms) :- keys_sample[shared](K, A), anew_ms_lower_measured[shared](T), Ms is T * (A - K) / A.
-- measured: with every key kept the evaluation did not move (65.5 s, the heap 470 MB more: anew a key is met once);
-- with the last 131 072 kept, 56.3 s anew and the delta 14.2 s (19.0)
anew_ms_keys_measured[shared](56313). delta_ms_keys_measured[shared](14187).

-- THE WORK CUT BY FILE (the owner's choice, 2026-11-12): one store; what a rule that never leaves a file concludes is
-- derived a file at a time on the workers, and the rules that cross files fire once over all of it. Counted anew
-- (the ledger says how): firings of the lower stage, of the rules above it that never left a file, of those that did.
firings[byfile](lower, 5611395). firings[byfile](in_file, 5480949). firings[byfile](across, 3515269).
-- the evaluation above the lower stage is 36 s of the 56 (38 samples of 60); its share by firings goes to the
-- workers, but what they conclude is taken into the store on one thread, at about what concluding costs (a third)
upper_ms[byfile](36000). whole_ms[byfile](56313). taking_share[byfile](33).
in_file_ms[byfile](Ms)  :- firings[byfile](in_file, I), firings[byfile](across, X), upper_ms[byfile](U), Ms is U * I / (I + X).
anew_ms[byfile](Ms)     :- in_file_ms[byfile](L), whole_ms[byfile](W), taking_share[byfile](T), threads[shared](C), Ms is W - L + L * (100 - T) / 100 / C + L * T / 100.
byfile_pays[byfile](Ms) :- anew_ms[byfile](Ms), anew_ms_volumes[shared](V), Ms < V.
-- BY THE RULES' SHAPE (own[fixpointplan] of the tree's facts, engine/stages.rs `rule_reach`) fewer rules are of one
-- file than never left one: 190 with 4 426 062 firings; the other 85 read what may cross (need: glob_of, denotes).
firings[byfile](by_shape, 4426062). firings[byfile](not_by_shape, 4570156).
shape_ms[byfile](Ms)      :- firings[byfile](by_shape, I), firings[byfile](not_by_shape, X), upper_ms[byfile](U), Ms is U * I / (I + X).
anew_ms_shape[byfile](Ms) :- shape_ms[byfile](L), whole_ms[byfile](W), taking_share[byfile](T), threads[shared](C), Ms is W - L + L * (100 - T) / 100 / C + L * T / 100.
-- MEASURED (the ledger: f_the_rules_of_one_file_are_derived_in_its_world): 49.9 s anew, 8.2 s the delta. Firings did
-- not say time: by the engine's own time by rule the rules of one file were 14.1 s of 35.7, not 17.7 of 36.
anew_ms_byfile_measured[byfile](49924). delta_ms_byfile_measured[byfile](8160).
rule_ms[byfile](of_file, 14112). rule_ms[byfile](across, 21629).
-- the same stage under the volumes' four workers (the default path): 31.7 s anew against 50, 7.3 s the delta against 15
anew_ms_byfile_volumes[byfile](31676). delta_ms_byfile_volumes[byfile](7279).

-- THE WRITING CUT BY A HASH OF THE ADDRESS (the owner, 2026-11-13). One worker after the files' part, by samples:
-- of 34 s the writing is 14, the search left on one thread 9, the rest 8. A worker writes the facts whose key hashes
-- to it; taking a round's conclusions apart by hash and putting the stretches together is counted as a tenth.
whole_ms[byhash](48600). serial_ms[byhash](writing, 14000). serial_ms[byhash](search, 9000). serial_ms[byhash](rest, 8000).
cut_ms[byhash](Part, Ms)  :- serial_ms[byhash](Part, S), threads[shared](C), Ms is S / C + S / 10.
anew_ms[byhash](writing, Ms) :- whole_ms[byhash](W), serial_ms[byhash](writing, S), cut_ms[byhash](writing, X), Ms is W - S + X.
anew_ms[byhash](search, Ms)  :- anew_ms[byhash](writing, A), serial_ms[byhash](search, S), cut_ms[byhash](search, X), Ms is A - S + X.
-- JUDGED 2026-11-13, AND THE FORECAST ABOVE FALLS WITH ITS MEASURE. The 14 s of writing were gdb samples; timers
-- in the engine itself say of one run anew (46 s): the files' part 15 s on four threads, the upper pass 25 s on one,
-- the rest 5 (indexed for retraction, kept, answered). In the upper pass the rules take 19 s: the search 12.5, the
-- writing of 4.05M solutions 5.4. Three trials of the writing moved nothing: the fact looked up on the threads
-- before it is written (forecast 45 s, got 48), the table of tuples half as full (the probe steps 4.6 to 1.1 a call,
-- the time the same), no table of tuples at all (the same).
upper_ms[bytimer](search, 12500). upper_ms[bytimer](writing, 5400). upper_ms[bytimer](rest, 7000).
refuted[byhash](found, 45000, 48000).
-- WHERE THE SEARCH IS ONE THREAD'S: a premise the threads do not take. `enters` by the news of does_fn reads
-- in_fn, a closure walked: 74 000 news gave 9.4M rows on one thread in 2.6 s, and 3.4M more in 0.6. The forecast
-- for the walked premise read on the threads: those 3.3 s on four threads and a tenth of them to hand out, and
-- what else stops at a walk (3.0M partial solutions) the same way.
walked_ms[bytimer](3300).
anew_ms[bytimer](walked, Ms) :- threads[shared](C), walked_ms[bytimer](S), Ms is 46500 - S + S / C + S / 10.
measured_ms[bytimer](walked, 42200).
-- (in pairs, the build before and this in turn, medians of three: 54.2 s to 51.1, and the four volumes 44.2 to 41.2)
paired_ms[bytimer](one, 54200, 51100). paired_ms[bytimer](volumes, 44200, 41200).
-- A ROUND SEARCHED AHEAD on the threads (every firing that starts from its news, before any is concluded): forecast
-- from the 8 s of search one thread still did, a share of 3 s; in pairs 45.5 s without and 46.0 with. The heavy
-- firings were on the threads already; the small ones are little together. Taken out.
refuted[bytimer](ahead, 42500, 46000).
